&=\dfrac{-3-\sqrt{17}}{2\times 2}\\
&=\dfrac{-3-\sqrt{17}}{4}
\end{aligned}
$$
et
$$\begin{aligned}
x_2&=\dfrac{-b+\sqrt{\Delta}}{2a}\\
&=\dfrac{-3+\sqrt{17}}{2\times 2}\\
&=\dfrac{-3+\sqrt{17}}{4}
\end{aligned}
$$
Donc $ S=\left\{ \dfrac{-3-\sqrt{17}}{4};\dfrac{-3+\sqrt{17}}{4}\right\}.$

